// Karimu Water Assets registry — embedded so the Ward/Village/Sub-Village/
// Asset Tag picker (and the volunteer route/map screen) work fully offline,
// matching the rest of this app's offline-first design.
//
// Source: Karimu "Water Assets" Google Sheet, "Water Assets" tab
// (https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1HLnqnP8wUJjV-MfVO9o7cio693qG220MpOHbFLRLrFE),
// exported 2026-08-25. 1,717 assets across the Ayalagaya, Arri, and Kiru
// wards — 1,693 Water Points and 24 Water Tanks. Only the Water Points are
// surfaced in the picker right now (see the filter on WATER_ASSETS below).
// Re-export and regenerate this file whenever the sheet changes
// significantly (new water points, renamed villages, new GPS coordinates).
//
// Each row is a tuple to keep this file's size down:
//   [assetTag, assetType, ward, village, subVillage, location,
//    lat, lon, volunteer, routeOrder]
// assetType is "P" for Water Point or "T" for Water Tank — this decides
// which checklist (WATER_POINT_SECTIONS or WATER_TANK_SECTIONS) applies.
// ward/village/subVillage/location are the raw values from the sheet;
// two Kiru assets have no village/sub-village on file and use "".
//
// lat/lon come from the sheet's "Coordinates in decimal" column and are
// null when that column was blank there — true for 572 of the 1,693 Water
// Points (34%), concentrated in villages that just weren't GPS-tagged yet
// (see README's "Volunteer routes" section). volunteer/routeOrder are
// precomputed here (not at runtime) so every device shows the exact same
// assignment: the 1,121 Water Points that do have coordinates were split
// into 6 roughly-equal, geographically-compact groups (a recursive
// median-cut partition — repeatedly slice the point cloud in half along
// whichever axis, lat or lon, currently spans further, so each half stays
// a compact geographic block instead of a scattered pick) and each group
// assigned to one volunteer, west to east. routeOrder is that volunteer's
// visiting order within their group, chosen by a nearest-neighbor walk
// starting from the westmost point — straight-line distance, since there's
// no detailed road network to route against out here. Water Points with no
// coordinates get a volunteer by majority vote of their own village's
// coordinate-bearing points (falling back to ward, then to the single
// largest group) and routeOrder null — the app lists them after the
// ordered route, unordered, since there's no coordinate to place them by.
// Water Tanks are out of scope for routing right now (see the Water Point
// filter below) and always carry volunteer/routeOrder null.

